; worldbadsave.eval - a save naming a member or a pack the party cannot have is
; refused, and the game goes on (code-review C349). Judged by tools/WorldTest.py
; phase 22, which writes the bad slot between runs: a copy of a good save with
; one hand-edited line added - `char -1 ...` on one run, `packc 0 -1 ...` on the
; next.
;
; Such a line used to resize the party to its index plus one (a -1 emptied it)
; and the next subscript read past the end: a debug abort, undefined in release.
; The good save loads first, as the control: the bad one differs from it by that
; one line alone.
logecho on
reset
load worldsaves_a
expect-refuse load worldsaves_bad
state
